    {
      "id": "p0146-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The translator explained the idea behind this localization change in the translation spreadsheet. Basically, in Japan, it's more common to stamp an important document with a hanko (a personalized ink seal) than with a signature. But if a hanlw isn't available when filling out an important document, a thumbprint is usually an acceptable alternative.",
